SWEET THERMAL hot mask by topology (patch 0402, follow-up of 0336; oriole speed round 2026-11-19, plan step 1.4). 0336's X1 drop applies mask 0x18 (boot & 0x18), which is the A76 pair only under tools/xrun's cpus=5 X1-first /cpus order. The oriole daily image runs cpus=8 in the plain DT order, where 0x18 = logical cpu3 (A55) + cpu4 (A76): two cores until <= 44 C (doc 56 Step 7, run wlan-gpu-o-all2). New pure th_hot_mask() in bsd/dev/sweet_thermal.h: the boot mask without every logical cpu whose physical core (topology phys_id Aff1, gs101 A55 0-3 / A76 4-5 / X1 6-7) is an X1; 0 = keep 0336's mask when the topology is unknown, when 0336's order check is clean (cpus=5 xrun order, 0x18 is the A76 pair), when no X1 is in the boot mask, or when fewer than TH_HOT_MIN_CORES (3) cores would stay (user 2026-11-19: never drop to two cores). Glue: th_check_cpu_order() stores it (th_hot_new) and prints 'SWEET THERMAL: hot mask 0x.. (patch 0402: ...)' when it is used; th_op_x1() applies it on the drop (restore = the boot mask, unchanged); the 'on' line shows the mask in use. Example: cpus=8 plain order with sweetrecores=0xfe -> 0x3e (A55 1-3 + A76 4-5). Unchanged: the thresholds (48 / 44 C), the charge hold, the 55 C CRIT park, every scheduler call is the same 0270 hint (no register). Host tests: tools/sweet_thermal_host_test.c (hot_* cases) and tools/sweet_thermal_glue_test.c (hot_dt8_*, hot_xrun8_drop_f9, hot_xrun5_no_hot_line) via tools/test_sweet_thermal.py.
